<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumbawa Besar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumbawa">Sumbawa</a> Besar is the main town of western Sumbawa in the Indonesian province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-nusa-tenggara">West Nusa Tenggara</a>. From the later 17th century it was the seat of the Sumbawa Sultanate, whose rulers intermarried with the royal families of Makassar and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> and accepted the overlordship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a>. Its royal palace, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istana-dalam-loka">Istana Dalam Loka</a>, dates from 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumbawa-besar.jpg" alt="Sumbawa Besar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MosheA · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DowntownSumbawa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
